// code_fpga_gt.vmem
// Hand-assembled RV32E(MC)-compatible program for the FPGA bring-up of the Grouper<->Trouper
// AHB integration (fpga_top.v). Loaded into Grouper's ahb_rom.sv via `include `PROG_FILE_VMEM
// for simulation (see ../scripts/run.sh); code_fpga_gt.hex is the $readmemh twin used when
// `FPGA is defined (Vivado build, see ../vivado/create_project.tcl).
//
// Only uses x1-x10 (within RV32E's 16-register x0-x15 limit) and plain 32-bit encodings
// (COMPRESSED_ISA=1 only permits 16-bit opcodes, doesn't require them) -- same convention as
// ../../fw/code_grouper_trouper.vmem. Assembled with a throwaway two-pass RV32I encoder
// (not committed) whose lui/addi/sb output was cross-checked byte-for-byte against that known-
// good reference file before use.
//
// Register conventions:
//   x1  = Trouper AHB window base (0x0001_0000)
//   x2  = ahb_gpio_dbg base (0x0002_0000): +0x00 SPI_CTRL {MOSI,SCK,CS_n,-,MISO}, +0x04 STATUS
//   x6  = MIMO_CTRL test value (0xF1) -- matches the value already proven safe to write in
//         Trouper's own tb_trouper_grp_arb.v (antenna_en=1111, mimo_mode=01)
//   x7  = SPI readback accumulator
//   x8  = SPI command byte shift register ({read=1, addr[6:0]} = 0x88 for MIMO_CTRL)
//
// Program flow:
//   1. AHB write: mem[0x10008] = 0xF1  (Trouper MIMO_CTRL over the real AHB3-Lite link)
//   2. Idle the bit-banged SPI lines, settle delay
//   3. One throwaway priming SPI read of MIMO_CTRL, discarded -- works around the same
//      spi_slave.v first-transaction-reads-garbage quirk documented/worked around in
//      tb_grouper_trouper_top.v (a Trouper-side quirk, not introduced by this bring-up)
//   4. Real independent SPI readback of MIMO_CTRL (same register, same bus, but via Trouper's
//      SPI slave port rather than the AHB path -- an oracle that can't be fooled by an AHB bug)
//   5. Compare to 0xF1; latch DONE|PASS (0x3) or DONE|FAIL (0x5) into ahb_gpio_dbg's STATUS
//      register, which drives led_status directly
//   6. Halt in a self-loop (testbench/ILA capture just samples led/status after the fact)
assign memory[ 'h00 ] = 32'h000100b7;
assign memory[ 'h01 ] = 32'h00020137;
assign memory[ 'h02 ] = 32'h0f100313;
